// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_setreg_on_restore.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: D-B — the restore's fire carries the restore ONLY (spec §4.2a).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "carries the restore ONLY"
//
// A well-formed band with a register write COMPOSED onto its restore's own line. It
// passes every OTHER guard, which is the point: the ops come out in prefix order (compose
// emits every SetReg before every stream op, so check_mixed_fire is satisfied by
// construction), two ops is inside the per-fire ceiling of four, one stream op is inside
// the ceiling of two, three words is exactly RASTER_BURST_MAX_DEEP, and the band's
// ownership is intact — same id on both records, equal spans, ON above the restore.
//
// It is still wrong, and item 1c sharpened rather than removed the reason. The spin solver
// would re-time this restore rather than mis-time it — but a restore is the deepest-dispatch
// op with the widest legal burst, so it starts with the least slack of anything in the DSL,
// and a register write ahead of it halves its solved spin. The de-mix pair for an S/H band
// is a reg_set a line ABOVE and the restore alone on the bottom line, which keeps that
// placement unconditional.
//
// IT IS ALSO THE STANDING WITNESS THAT THE BAND ID SURVIVES `compose` (band-ownership
// design §2.1). compose REBUILDS every merged fire, so a mark carried on the FIRE would be
// lost here — the merged record at line 140 is a fresh RasterFire.Fire. The mark is on the
// OP, and ops are copied verbatim by both of compose's passes, so the restore arrives at
// the ownership walk still carrying its band's id. If that ever stopped being true this
// poison would report an ownership sentence beside D-B's, and the count below would say so.
//
// COUNT 1: D-B alone.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_two_restores.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_setreg_on_restore

const POISON_SETREG_ON_RESTORE = compose([
    band(100, 140, stream_cram($48, [$0EEE, $0AAA, $0666]), 0),
    [ fire(140, [reg_set($8C81)]) ],
])

ensure(raster_program(POISON_SETREG_ON_RESTORE).len > 0,
       "poison_setreg_on_restore: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
